window.__T__=[{"i":18720,"text":"```\n围绕任意主题对象生成品牌视觉风格板，整体先建立上下强明度分区：上部是干净高明度空白场，放置主题相关的真实物件或材质样本，采用俯视陈列和轻微错位的斜向交叉关系，让长条、圆头、尖端或弯曲轮廓形成可被提炼的符号线索；物件保留手工痕迹、磨损边、暗部擦亮、局部裂纹或涂层剥落，阴影柔软贴地，空白面积大于实物占用，使粗粝材质显得安静而被审视。下部转入低明度哑黑信息场，顶部只放少量极小字距的说明文字，左右边角形成轻微对称，中轴放简短中文名与小号英文转写，保持留白压住信息密度。主要标志从上部物件的轮廓中提炼，不直接复制物件，而把主题的长柄、圆端、凹口、缺角、连接处转化为松散手写字母和幼拙图形，字母大小不齐、基线跳动、间距松散，局部字形被器物状剪影替代，像手剪纸片或厚涂颜料贴在黑底上。配色按主题自适应：高明度底色与低明度底色承担大面积结构，标志使用少量低饱和主题色与暖白色形成明暗跳点，彩色版和浅色版并置时保持同一字形骨架。避免精致矢量、商业光泽和整齐网格，必须保留朴拙、手作、材料磨耗、图形与文字互相变形的关系。\n\n——————\n为旧物修补材料品牌建立视觉风格板：上部高明度空场陈列补丁布、针线、胶带和磨损边角，采用近似圆环的聚拢构图，中间留出一块安静空白；以砖红作为唯一低饱和强调色，暖白、哑黑与灰褐承担主体，材质依旧粗粝而无光泽。标志置于下部黑场中轴，标题做窄长竖向排列，英文转写拆成两段贴近字形轮廓，信息层级从标题到微小注释逐级收缩；画幅为竖版 3:4。\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrgSeEboAEy7Pq.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrgZ27bcAA9meG.jpg"]},{"i":18721,"text":"不然做样张，真的容易废片\n\n本组提示词：\n```\n将任意未来主题构造成一张冷峻、实验性的纪实活动海报：第一眼必须是被高速运动模糊吞没的主体，与一组巨大、垂直或横向切入画面的标题字形成强烈叠压，文字既是信息也是遮挡、切割和视觉重量。采用近乎黑白的冷灰单色印刷感，以深黑块、雾灰影像和白色字形建立硬朗明暗秩序，只允许极少量主题相关色彩作为克制的识别点。画面以偏置轴线、局部裁切和大面积不均匀留白组织阅读路径：主标题占据边缘或穿过主体，辅助信息沿另一条清晰轴线分层排列，避免居中对称和平均分布。背景与主题内容应通过真实动作、拖影、失焦、压缩颗粒或粗糙纸面共同生成，图像边缘、文字边缘和底材共享轻微的灰阶扩散、叠印错位与透明覆盖，使文字仿佛在影像内部移动，而不是后期贴上去。字体采用窄体、几何、机械感强的无衬线构造：高而紧的字面、明确的骨架、克制的圆角或直切端点、紧密字距和稳定重复节奏；粗体标题与细体说明形成尺度落差，字形可被裁切、旋转或沿边界排列，但仍保持跨文字系统的可读性。保留少量网格线、定位标记或版面辅助痕迹作为制作证据，细节只服务于层级和动势。禁止鲜艳渐变、过度锐化、装饰性插画、奢华材质、干净无瑕的商业模板和无理由的复古做旧；主题变化时重建主体形态与信息内容，但固定运动影像、巨大叠字、冷灰印刷、偏置裁切和共享墨色质感之间的因果关系。\n\n——————\n把它做成工业设计论坛活动海报：以蓝灰、炭黑和少量冷黄标记色构成硬朗印刷层次，机械结构的局部运动模糊从右上向左下贯穿画面，细密网格和定位标记集中在下半部，上方保留不规则冷灰留白；标题采用顶部横向窄体巨字，说明文字缩小并沿底部基线排列，让信息从上到下形成清晰的工程化节奏。画幅为竖版 3:4。\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrhvQca8AAvCpc.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrhvQhbAAAzxkC.jpg"]},{"i":18722,"text":"```\n让未来主题先被压缩成一组可辨识的主体影像，再把影像完整嵌入占据画面核心的大型窄长粗体字中：第一眼看到的不是独立照片与标题，而是文字轮廓、内部景象和黑色留白共同形成的巨大视觉切片。字形承担主要构图，竖向笔画密集排列，横向空间被压缩，字与字之间保留硬朗、近乎机械的黑色间隙；内部图像在不同字腔中连续错位，但仍共享同一条景深、地平线或动作路径，使阅读、观看和主题叙事同时发生。主题内容应重建为具有远近层次、明确主体尺度和局部动作的纪实场景，人物或物件只作为影像中的尺度锚点，不单独抢夺标题层级。背景使用近乎纯黑的平面，外围留白克制，底部安静排列少量等宽、技术感强的说明文字、地点信息或符号标记，形成主视觉下方的资料档案感。色彩以黑底和低饱和冷色影像为骨架，允许主题自身提供少量自然色，但整体保持偏灰、偏冷、低装饰；光线像户外纪实摄影，明暗由真实景物决定，不添加商业渐变。字内图像与字形边缘应有轻微裁切、压缩和印刷转译感，局部细节可粗糙但不能脏乱，保留清晰识别度、硬边和不完全均匀的图文贴合。字体不是指定字库：使用可迁移的窄体高字面结构、厚重直线笔画、紧凑字距、浅窄内腔、简洁端点与少量锐利转折；让不同文字系统根据自身字形拓扑重新组织笔画、字腔、连接和阅读节奏，确保目标文字仍能自然辨认。避免把照片缩成普通背景、让标题浮在图片上、过度美化、圆润可爱、丰富装饰、柔焦、霓虹、渐变背景或整齐无菌的数字排版。\n\n——————\n将主题落地为高原输电线路巡检海报：以岩石赭褐为主色，叠加铅灰、低饱和青绿与微弱的安全黄，低角度侧光强化真实地形；巨型窄长字横向分成两组，内部影像沿斜向电塔—山脊—巡检人员路径错位衔接，主体集中在左下并向右上展开，黑色留白压住四周密度；标题采用左上小字引导、中央超大字承重、底部技术资料次级排列的三级层级，画幅为竖版 3:4。\n\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrjuOUawAATQT7.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrjuOLbgAAp_kd.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrjuOabwAAPFok.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTrkSTpakAAfCyp.jpg"]},{"i":18723,"text":"Create a premium 3:4 vertical collectible travel poster for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\nCreate a sophisticated 3D travel souvenir poster featuring a charming contemporary character sitting on the bottom edge of a large Polaroid-style photo frame, with one leg naturally extending outside the frame to create a playful dimensional pop-out effect. The character holds a smartphone and takes a fun, natural selfie.\n\nINSIDE THE POLAROID\nFill the Polaroid with a vibrant, cinematic travel scene that instantly communicates the identity of [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Automatically combine its most recognizable landmark, architecture, landscapes, local food, traditional crafts, transportation, street life, nature, and everyday cultural details into one cohesive environment.\n\nThe character's clothing, accessories, colors, and styling should subtly reflect the destination's contemporary culture without becoming stereotypical. Keep the expression cheerful, relaxed, and natural.\n\nOUTSIDE THE FRAME\nCreate a premium soft gradient background inspired by the destination's visual identity. Surround the Polaroid with elegant monochrome hand-drawn travel illustrations and small graphic icons representing meaningful landmarks, local food, flora and fauna, transportation, maps, traditional motifs, architecture, and cultural details.\n\nKeep the surrounding illustrations delicate and secondary, with generous negative space and a clean editorial composition.\n\nTYPOGRAPHY\nPlace the destination name prominently at the top in stylish expressive handwritten or editorial lettering. Add a small destination-inspired symbol or flag where appropriate.\n\nInclude a short elegant travel slogan near the bottom and one brief handwritten inspirational travel phrase. Keep typography refined, minimal, and integrated into the composition.\n\nSTYLE & LIGHTING\nPremium collectible tourist poster × polished 3D illustration × realistic miniature depth × contemporary editorial design × playful character storytelling.\n\nUse soft cinematic lighting, realistic materials, subtle depth of field, tactile textures, dimensional shadows, vibrant but tasteful destination-inspired colors, and refined print-quality detailing.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\nA sophisticated travel souvenir that feels playful, premium, memorable, and instantly connected to [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] through its architecture, nature, food, fashion, colors, culture, and everyday atmosphere.\n\nAvoid stereotypes, generic scenery, clutter, excessive typography, flat vector graphics, distorted anatomy, awkward hands, floating objects, random landmarks, logos, watermarks, UI elements, and overly cartoonish rendering.\n\nFORMAT\n3:4 vertical poster, single cohesive composition, highly detailed 3D rendering, polished editorial quality, realistic textures, cinematic depth, premium social-media-ready artwork.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTruzYFb0AAhB3d.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTru0GTaQAAqWCt.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTru1CTa0AAXCB9.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTru2ShaIAAj7n6.jpg"]},{"i":18724,"text":"Use the uploaded reference photo as the primary visual reference and transform it into a premium “real-life moment + illustrated memory board” editorial poster.\n\nCreate a vertical 3:4 composition divided horizontally into two equal sections.\n\nTOP HALF — REALISTIC PHOTO:\nPreserve the original subject, face, identity, hairstyle, clothing, pose, body proportions, objects, and environment from the reference image. Keep the scene highly photorealistic with natural skin texture, realistic lighting, soft cinematic depth of field, subtle warm tones, and an elegant lifestyle/editorial photography aesthetic. Do not change the person’s identity or outfit unnecessarily.\n\nBOTTOM HALF — HAND-DRAWN MEMORY COLLAGE:\nConvert the important visual elements from the top photograph into a charming hand-drawn fashion/lifestyle scrapbook illustration. Recreate the subject as a delicate colored-pencil and watercolor sketch, along with the key objects, clothing, accessories, flowers, food/drinks, furniture, architecture, books, artwork, or other recognizable details from the scene.\n\nArrange these illustrated elements organically across a warm ivory/off-white textured paper background. Use delicate pencil outlines, subtle watercolor washes, imperfect hand-drawn strokes, soft pastel accents, light pink/blue/green sketch marks, tiny hearts, doodles, and understated decorative elements. Keep the illustrations elegant, minimal, nostalgic, and handmade rather than cartoonish.\n\nAdd a small handwritten cursive title near the top of the illustrated section that reflects the mood of the original photo, such as “little moments,” “slow morning,” “a little memory,” or another context-appropriate phrase. Add very small handwritten decorative text near the bottom.\n\nThe illustrated section should feel like a personal visual diary / fashion magazine scrapbook / memory journal, while still clearly connecting every illustrated element to the original photograph.\n\nStyle: sophisticated editorial scrapbook, colored-pencil illustration, delicate watercolor, vintage paper texture, cozy lifestyle aesthetic, soft pastel palette, subtle imperfections, elegant composition, premium Pinterest/editorial design, nostalgic and artistic.\n\nComposition: clean spacing, balanced negative space, no clutter, seamless transition between the realistic photograph and illustrated memory section, realistic top half + hand-drawn bottom half, high detail, natural proportions.\n\nImportant: Keep the original photo recognizable and preserve the subject’s identity and major visual details. Do not introduce unrelated objects. Avoid excessive text, logos, borders, stickers, or cartoon-style rendering.\n\nShorter version\n\nTransform the uploaded photo into a 3:4 premium “real photo + illustrated memory scrapbook” poster. Keep the top 50% as a highly realistic version of the original photo, preserving the subject’s identity, pose, clothing, environment, lighting, and important details. Convert the bottom 50% into a warm ivory paper collage containing hand-drawn colored-pencil and watercolor illustrations of the subject and the key objects, outfits, accessories, flowers, furniture, architecture, books, and other details from the photo. Add delicate pastel scribbles, tiny hearts, subtle doodles, soft paper texture, and elegant handwritten cursive text such as “little moments” or “slow morning.” Sophisticated editorial lifestyle scrapbook aesthetic, nostalgic, handmade, refined, soft pastel colors, clean composition, premium Pinterest-style design, realistic top / artistic illustrated bottom, no unrelated elements, no excessive text.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTsJlHjaYAARHFg.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTsJlHPbAAAITSm.jpg"]},{"i":18725,"text":"Create a vertical cozy home scrapbook poster inspired by the reference images. Combine a beautiful realistic interior photograph on the top half with a hand-drawn illustrated memory journal on the bottom half.\n\nTop section: A warm, bright and minimalist cozy home interior with natural cream walls, light wooden furniture, open wooden shelves filled with tiny ceramic houses, cute collectible figurines, miniature animals, books, framed artwork and handmade décor. Include a wooden desk or dining table, vintage radio, small lamp, flowers, baskets, ceramics and carefully arranged little objects. Soft sunlight streaming through the window, warm natural shadows, peaceful Scandinavian/Japanese cottage aesthetic, clean and inviting, realistic interior photography, highly detailed.\n\nBottom section: Transform the same room and objects into a charming hand-drawn scrapbook illustration on textured warm cream paper. Arrange the illustrations in a neat 3×3 grid, with each small panel showing a cozy detail: miniature houses, cute character figures, vintage radio, tablet/screen, table lamp, tiny animal collection, flower vase, ceramic collection, baskets, books and other little decorations. Use delicate watercolor and colored-pencil textures, soft brown ink outlines, muted pastel colors, slightly imperfect handmade strokes.\n\nAdd a handwritten title at the top: “My Little World” or “My Cozy Home”, with tiny stars, hearts and simple doodles. Add short handwritten captions beneath each illustration, such as “little things, big happiness,” “cozy corner,” “my little collection,” “warm light,” “home sweet home,” “small moments, big joy.”\n\nStyle: cozy lifestyle magazine + handmade travel journal, nostalgic scrapbook, watercolor and colored-pencil illustration, textured paper, warm beige and natural wood tones, soft sunlight, cute miniature details, elegant minimal composition, highly detailed, vertical 4:5 poster, seamless transition from realistic photography to illustration, no watermark.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTsZQ-ybEAAWXow.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTsZQ7sacAAG1N-.jpg"]},{"i":18726,"text":"Create a premium 3:4 vertical cinematic travel poster for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\nCreate an elegant, photorealistic travel editorial inspired by luxury tourism campaigns, high-end fashion magazines, cinematic photography, and premium airline advertising. Use a warm ivory-to-soft-white background with generous negative space, refined composition, and a quiet sophisticated atmosphere.\n\nCHARACTER & POSE\nFeature one contemporary traveler as the main subject, positioned slightly off-center and captured full-body in a natural three-quarter side profile. The traveler is casually walking through the destination, creating an effortless candid travel moment rather than a posed portrait.\n\nGive the traveler a small vintage camera held naturally in one hand, with the other hand carrying a compact leather travel bag or resting casually near the shoulder. The posture should feel relaxed, authentic, and elegant.\n\nAutomatically style the traveler according to the destination: refined contemporary travel clothing, appropriate seasonal layers, tasteful neutral tones, practical footwear, and subtle accessories inspired by the local environment without becoming stereotypical.\n\nDESTINATION STORY\nBuild the background around the visual identity of [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Automatically select the most recognizable landmark, architecture, streetscape, landscape, cultural details, and environmental elements that genuinely belong to the destination.\n\nKeep the environment realistic and photographically believable. Add subtle local details that make the destination immediately recognizable while maintaining a clean editorial composition.\n\nLIGHTING & ATMOSPHERE\nSoft warm autumn or late-afternoon sunlight, delicate golden rim light, gentle atmospheric haze, realistic skin and fabric textures, subtle shadows, restrained contrast, and cinematic natural illumination.\n\nSTYLE\nLuxury travel editorial × cinematic destination photography × high-end airline campaign × contemporary fashion magazine × fine-art photography.\n\nUse realistic photographic detail, natural proportions, sophisticated depth of field, subtle film grain, restrained saturation, and a calm premium visual language.\n\nCOLOR PALETTE\nWarm ivory, cream, soft beige, muted earth tones, charcoal, and destination-specific accent colors. Keep saturation low to medium and maintain a refined monochromatic harmony.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\nQuiet luxury travel photography, sophisticated autumn atmosphere, authentic human presence, premium editorial storytelling, timeless composition, and a polished collectible travel-poster feeling.\n\nAvoid crowded scenes, exaggerated poses, stereotypes, fantasy architecture, excessive colors, heavy HDR, oversaturated grading, artificial skin, distorted anatomy, duplicate people, logos, watermarks, UI elements, and excessive typography.\n\nFORMAT\n3:4 vertical, full-body character, cinematic composition, generous negative space, photorealistic detail, premium editorial quality, single cohesive image.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTtGNE7a4AABBeI.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTtGN1sbQAAE_mC.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTtGOhIaYAAEYyM.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTtGPJdbgAA9WJo.jpg"]},{"i":18727,"text":"Create a highly aesthetic, cinematic poster of [LANDMARK] transformed into an unmistakable October atmosphere — rich burnt orange, deep rust, muted amber, and warm brown tones, crisp autumn air, swirling maple leaves naturally framing the landmark, soft golden-hour sunlight, subtle mist, cozy street lamps glowing, wet stone streets reflecting warm light, a few scattered pumpkins and autumn details integrated tastefully into the environment.\n\nKeep the landmark instantly recognizable and visually dominant, while making the entire scene feel like a frame from a premium autumn movie. Add subtle film grain, realistic paper texture, atmospheric depth, dramatic shadows, sophisticated editorial composition, and a slightly nostalgic 35mm photography feel.\n\nNo Halloween clichés, no cartoon look, no excessive decorations. Make it elegant, cinematic, mysterious, and highly shareable — the kind of October visual that feels like “the landmark entered its autumn era.”\n\nMinimal refined typography: “OCTOBER” with a small location name underneath. Vertical 4:5 poster composition, premium travel-editorial aesthetic, viral Pinterest/Instagram visuals","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTw9QHJaQAA4XaX.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTw9QyOacAEbzK3.jpg"]},{"i":18728,"text":"Create a premium 2:3 vertical architectural poster for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK]. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\nPresent [LANDMARK] as an expressive unfinished architectural master sketch, as if drawn by an architect exploring the building’s form, structure, and character. Keep the real architecture accurate — preserve its recognizable silhouette, proportions, façade rhythm, materials, and signature details. Do not redesign the landmark.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nShow approximately 80–95% of the landmark from the most elegant and architecturally informative viewpoint for that specific building. Use a natural eye-level or gently elevated three-quarter perspective with realistic depth and restrained distortion.\n\nONE LANDMARK ONLY. Let it dominate the composition while surrounding it with generous PURE WHITE negative space. No skyline or secondary landmarks.\n\nSKETCH STYLE\nCombine precise architectural ink drawing with loose unfinished concept-sketch elements:\n\ncrisp black structural lines\n\nfine façade detailing\n\nvaried line weights\n\nconstruction and perspective guides\n\nsubtle drafting marks\n\nselective ink washes\n\npartially unfinished contours\n\nSome areas should be highly detailed while others naturally dissolve into loose exploratory lines and white space. It must feel genuinely hand-drawn, not like a 3D render with a sketch filter.\n\nDETAIL & COLOR\nReveal authentic architectural elements such as structural connections, façade layers, openings, ornamentation, joints, and material textures. Never invent features that do not belong to the landmark.\n\nUse a PURE WHITE background with black and charcoal linework, plus ONE subtle accent color naturally derived from the landmark’s real materials.\n\nTYPOGRAPHY\nOptional small refined text in one corner:\n[DESTINATION]\n[LANDMARK]\n\nKeep typography minimal and secondary to the architecture.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\nArchitectural master sketch × technical drawing × expressive ink work × restrained hand-painted wash × contemporary collectible art poster.\n\nAvoid fictional architecture, incorrect proportions, extreme perspectives, close-ups, surrounding cityscapes, multiple landmarks, beige/aged paper, gradients, excessive colors, glossy 3D rendering, oversized typography, logos, and watermarks.\n\nFORMAT\n2:3 vertical, single landmark, full architectural form clearly visible, generous white space, intricate linework, natural perspective, premium gallery-quality finish.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTx1hkEakAEJiFP.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTx2EeiagAE_09t.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTx2Fv2awAAZZGx.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HTx2HUQaQAAvF0U.jpg"]},{"i":18729,"text":"Create a stunning premium architectural travel poster inspired by vintage architectural illustration, featuring [LANDMARK / CITY] as the hero subject.\n\nShow the landmark in an elegant three-quarter perspective, with extremely detailed hand-drawn architectural linework, intricate windows, balconies, columns, textures and ornamental details. Keep the sophisticated editorial composition of a collectible architecture magazine, but transform the artwork into a rich, bright, highly colorful illustration.\n\nUse a beautiful palette of coral red, vibrant turquoise, cobalt blue, sunny yellow, emerald green, warm orange, pink, lavender and golden accents, with natural color variation rather than flat digital blocks. Add colorful trees, flowers, pedestrians, bicycles, vintage cars, street signs and subtle city-life details around the architecture.\n\nBehind the landmark, include a delicate illustrated city map in pale pastel lines, architectural measurement marks, tiny street names and faint blueprint details. Add a small architectural detail sketch on one side, as if taken from an old design archive.\n\nAt the top, use refined typography:\n[CITY NAME]\n[LANDMARK NAME]\nsmall location coordinates beneath.\n\nAt the bottom, include elegant archival-style information such as EST. [YEAR] · ARCHITECTURAL STYLE · CITY · COUNTRY.\n\nThe overall image should feel like a luxury collectible travel poster, combining colored-pencil texture, watercolor washes, fine ink drawing, subtle wax-crayon grain and vintage print imperfections. Bright sunlight, glowing colors, crisp details, warm paper texture, sophisticated composition, beautiful depth, highly detailed yet artistic.\n\nAvoid: dull muted colors, photorealistic photography, generic cartoon style, excessive text, neon cyberpunk aesthetics, flat vector graphics.\n\nMood: joyful, colorful, cultured, nostalgic, sophisticated, artistic, instantly eye-catching, Pinterest-worthy and Instagram-viral.\n\nFor an even more striking result: make the architecture mostly detailed and realistic, while letting the trees, sky, flowers, cars and small street elements explode with bright color. That contrast will make the landmark pop without losing the elegant architectural-poster feel.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT1xfdHbAAEDXmd.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT1xfdAaEAApTG_.jpg"]},{"i":18730,"text":"Create a premium vintage Indian postage-stamp travel poster for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\nTransform the destination into a collectible vintage postage stamp, presenting its most iconic architecture, culture, landscape, and local character as a finely engraved travel illustration.\n\nSTAMP DESIGN\nCreate ONE centered postage stamp with authentic perforated edges and a subtle cream paper texture. Automatically select the most recognizable landmark or combination of visual elements that represents the destination.\n\nUse detailed engraved linework, delicate crosshatching, vintage print texture, and slightly imperfect ink registration for an authentic old-world postal aesthetic.\n\nINDIAN IDENTITY\nGive the stamp a refined Indian postal character with:\n- “भारत INDIA” as the header\n- ₹100 denomination\n- destination name in elegant Latin lettering\n- the destination name again in its appropriate regional script\n\nAdapt the regional script and cultural details accurately to the chosen location.\n\nCOLOR & COMPOSITION\nUse a restrained destination-inspired palette with 3–5 complementary vintage colors. Keep the cream paper visible around the artwork and maintain strong visual hierarchy.\n\nInclude only meaningful local details — architecture, landscape, traditional motifs, vegetation, transportation, or cultural elements that genuinely belong to the destination.\n\nSTYLE\nVintage Indian postage stamp × engraved illustration × heritage printmaking × collectible travel ephemera.\n\nThe result should feel authentic, minimal, timeless, sophisticated, and museum-worthy rather than like a modern digital poster.\n\nAvoid photorealism, glossy rendering, excessive colors, generic landmarks, invented cultural details, clutter, modern graphic effects, multiple separate stamps, logos, watermarks, and excessive text.\n\nFORMAT\nOne stamp per image, vertical composition, perforated border, cream paper texture, highly detailed engraving, elegant typography, premium collectible finish.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2A4vsaQAA80TD.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2A5r6b0AAoFXD.jpg"]},{"i":18731,"text":"Transform the uploaded photo into a premium travel-memory scrapbook poster.\n\nKeep the original photo as the main visual reference and preserve the important subjects, objects, environment, composition, colors, and recognizable details accurately. Do not change the identity or structure of the main subject.\n\nCreate a vertical 3:4 editorial scrapbook layout divided horizontally into two equal sections:\n\nTOP 50%:\nPlace the original photograph prominently, enhanced with warm, natural, slightly cinematic color grading. Keep it realistic, detailed, and photographic. Do not over-edit or make it look artificial.\n\nBOTTOM 50%:\nCreate a beautiful hand-drawn illustrated journal page inspired directly by the photograph. Extract 6–9 of the most recognizable visual elements from the original image and turn each into a small individual colored-pencil / ink / watercolor-style sketch arranged in a clean 3×3 scrapbook grid.\n\nUse:\n- textured warm ivory/off-white paper background\n- subtle paper grain\n- hand-drawn pencil and ink outlines\n- loose colored-pencil and watercolor shading\n- slightly imperfect handmade strokes\n- soft muted but cheerful colors\n- tiny doodles such as stars, hearts, leaves, sparkles, waves and arrows\n- thin, delicate hand-drawn grid dividers\n- cozy travel-journal aesthetic\n- sophisticated editorial composition\n- authentic handmade imperfections\n\nAdd a handwritten title at the top of the illustrated section, customized to the photo's theme, such as “[LOCATION] Memories”, “[THEME] Moments”, “Sweet Moments”, “Blue Sky Memories”, etc.\n\nUnder each illustrated element, add a short handwritten label describing it, for example:\n“street lamp”, “soft clouds”, “colorful lights”, “tea”, “old walls”, “sweet treat”, “green moments”, etc.\n\nAt the very bottom, add a small handwritten sentimental caption related to the photo, such as:\n“a perfect day to remember ♡”\nor\n“same place, different feelings ♡”\n\nThe final result should feel like a luxury travel scrapbook / visual diary page created by hand, combining a real photograph with charming illustrated memories.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- One original photo + one illustrated memory section\n- Clean 50/50 horizontal division\n- Vertical 3:4 composition\n- Preserve the original photo realistically\n- Illustrations must clearly originate from objects in the uploaded photo\n- No photorealistic illustrations\n- No 3D rendering\n- No excessive graphic-design effects\n- No borders around individual illustrations\n- No random objects unrelated to the photo\n- Keep typography minimal, elegant, and handwritten\n- Make the entire page cohesive, warm, nostalgic, artistic, and premium","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2GUrxacAAYY8O.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2GUrvagAAprXh.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2GUrzboAATHqM.jpg"]},{"i":18732,"text":"Premium Editorial Poster Instructions\n\nEach uploaded photo must be made into a separate, independent, premium editorial poster, and multiple photos must not be combined. Use a strict 3:4 vertical canvas. Split the canvas horizontally in the exact center: the upper half and the lower half each occupy 50% of the height, are equally wide, and equally high, with no alteration of proportion.\n\nThe upper half uses the original photo directly and must not be regenerated. Preserve the identity of the main subject, the human body or architectural structure, proportions, perspective, spatial relationships, texture, natural light and shadow, color, and environment in their entirety. Only slight cropping and restrained premium color grading are permitted; re-drawing the main subject, fictional light, HDR, excessive saturation, plastic texture, and fictional content are prohibited. hibited. When needing to adapt to the frame, only environmental areas such as sky, water surface, ground, walls, plants, or background can be extended.\n\nThe lower half extracts and reconstructs the \"narrative core\" of the photo: it can be a single primary subject, or a group of related elements that together embody the photo's identity, scale, action, o story relationship. Maintain its realistic, recognizable appearance, proportion, internal structure, texture, and relative position. Do not remove important related elements, and do not directly us rectangular photo cutouts. The reconstructed subject typically occupies 55%-80% of the width of the lower area. It should naturally extend based on the photo's primary direction and retain plausible ground, water lines, shadows, or softly dissipated edges to integrate into the background, avoiding a sticker-like or floating appearance.\n\nIncorporate a narrow, low-saturation geometric color field behind or through the center of the subject, serving as a \"critical window\" between reality and editorial abstraction. The color of the window must be extracted from the original photo, and its orientation (horizontal, vertical, or diagonal) chosen based on the overall narrative direction.\n\nThe subject must actively pass through the window: part of it is within the color field, and part enters the open negative space, naturally crossing the window's boundary to create occlusion, penetration, and spatial depth. The window is not a frame or a card; it must not fully enclose the subject. Only one primary window is allowed; multiple color blocks, thick borders, rounded corners, strong gradients, and drop shadows are prohibited.\n\nUse a white, cool white, very light gray, or near-white background for the lower half, coordinated with the photo. Employ a restrained asymmetrical composition and abundant negative space to establish a three-tier hierarchy:\n\nReconstructed subject or narrative composition\n\nLow-saturation geometric window","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2IoDPbEAA5gwo.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2IsSRbYAAcil_.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2IsSUagAAcBiQ.jpg"]},{"i":18733,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical on-location travel sketch of [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK], drawn in a small artist’s watercolor sketchbook.\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire scene creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\nCapture the chosen landmark as a spontaneous sketch made directly on location by a skilled travel artist. Preserve its recognizable silhouette, proportions, architecture, and defining features, but interpret them with quick, economical marks rather than fully rendering every detail.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nShow ONE natural street-level viewpoint, choosing the most characteristic perspective for the landmark. Include only a small amount of surrounding architecture, greenery, street elements, and a few tiny gestural figures where appropriate.\n\nLet the drawing naturally dissolve into untouched white paper around the edges. Keep the landmark as the clear focal point while allowing parts of the scene to remain unfinished.\n\nSKETCH STYLE\nUse loose observational urban-sketch techniques:\n- light wandering graphite construction lines\n- occasional confident dark ink accents\n- quick transparent watercolor washes\n- visible brushstrokes, blooms and pigment overlaps\n- irregular, broken and doubled lines\n- simplified architectural details\n- areas where watercolor crosses or escapes the linework\n- generous untouched paper\n\nConcentrate detail around the landmark’s most recognizable architectural features and allow secondary areas to fade into suggestive marks.\n\nCOLOR\nUse a small, restrained watercolor palette naturally derived from the real landmark and its surroundings. Keep the paper predominantly white and allow subtle variations, uneven washes, and accidental edges to remain visible.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\nAuthentic travel sketchbook × European urban sketching × loose watercolor × graphite observation × handmade artistic spontaneity.\n\nThe image should feel like a beautiful 20–30 minute sketch made while sitting in front of the landmark — observant, imperfect, intimate, and alive.\n\nAvoid photorealism, polished architectural rendering, overly precise linework, fully painted backgrounds, uniform detail, digital smoothness, heavy shading, excessive colors, decorative borders, text, logos, and watermarks.\n\nFORMAT\n4:5 vertical, single cohesive sketchbook page, natural street-level perspective, white paper, loose unfinished edges, expressive watercolor and graphite texture.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2-kwVbkAA1kFh.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2-liKbYAAzNRG.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2-mJhaUAEFwbQ.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2-m1MaIAAtyem.jpg"]},{"i":18734,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical retro psychedelic travel illustration for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\nReimagine the chosen landmark as a joyful 1960s–70s psychedelic pop travel illustration. Keep the landmark immediately recognizable and architecturally believable, but simplify it into bold graphic shapes, expressive contours, and playful color fields.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nPlace ONE iconic landmark as the clear focal point, using a clean three-quarter or natural frontal view that best suits its architecture. Surround it with a minimal stylized environment inspired by the destination — simple clouds, sun, hills, vegetation, water, or broad flowing ground shapes where appropriate.\n\nKeep the composition spacious and graphic. The landmark should dominate without becoming overly detailed.\n\nILLUSTRATION STYLE\nUse confident hand-drawn charcoal outlines with slightly irregular continuous contours. Make outer silhouettes stronger than internal architectural marks.\n\nCombine:\n- bold flat color fields\n- simplified architectural forms\n- organic clouds and shapes\n- broad flowing foreground bands\n- playful 1960s–70s graphic geometry\n- minimal internal detail\n- clean raster illustration\n\nThe artwork should feel screen-printed and handmade, not like a modern vector template or a photograph with a filter.\n\nCOLOR\nBuild a distinctive destination-inspired psychedelic palette with 4–6 bold colors. Use a warm light base tone plus contrasting saturated colors, while allowing the landmark itself to remain visually dominant.\n\nAutomatically choose colors that complement the destination rather than forcing the same palette onto every location.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\nRetro psychedelic pop × vintage travel poster × hand-drawn editorial illustration × 1960s–70s graphic design.\n\nCheerful, bold, nostalgic, playful, instantly recognizable, and visually striking.\n\nAvoid photorealism, 3D rendering, realistic textures, excessive architectural detail, generic scenery, gradients, glossy effects, texture overlays, clutter, modern corporate design, logos, watermarks, and excessive text.\n\nFORMAT\n4:5 vertical, one landmark, clean graphic composition, bold flat colors, strong hand-drawn contours, minimal background, premium poster-quality illustration.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT31ZNFbwAAYEv_.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT31Z94bsAApt0_.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT31avqawAA63Dc.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT31bicawAAEk__.jpg"]},{"i":18735,"text":"模型再怎么进化\n作图的需求还是摆在这里...\n只想作图功能：越来越利索、越来越美\n\n这波样张， 是之前做好在本地还没上传到提示词库\n但是快了，快了...\n因为我重新梳理了上架风格的流程\n\n本次提示词，汤底+佐料：\n```\n先建立一眼可辨的视觉事件：大面积低照度、近乎静止的深冷色环境占据主体空间，一个尺寸极小却明亮温暖的圆形焦点悬置在空场中，以极端尺度反差和冷暖反差压住全局；下部由更暗的水平基底与突然抬起、带颗粒和飞沫感的高能纹理形成第二重事件，让安静的远处与近处的猛烈运动同时存在。画面采用摄影纪实质感而非精修商业质感，暗青、墨蓝、黑褐构成窄色域，亮点呈克制的旧金色，局部高光偏灰白；保留轻微失焦、低清晰度、压暗阴影、模拟高感光噪点、微弱色偏和不均匀曝光，不添加华丽光晕、顺滑渐变或过度锐化。空间组织以上部巨大留白、下部密集信息为核心，地平式横向分界压低，运动纹理允许裁切出界；所有文字贴附于下方暗部和纹理交界，像杂志内页与私人日记叠印在照片上。主标题使用粗重、紧凑、低重心的无衬线构造，字形由宽厚近等粗笔画、短促平切端点、结实连接、较小内腔和紧密字距组成，可分成两行错位堆叠，并与翻涌纹理局部交叠；无论目标文字采用何种书写系统，都保持其正字法可识别性、原阅读方向与自然标记位置，以字面面积、笔画重量和节奏实现同等压迫感，不模仿某一种来源字母。辅助信息使用较轻但仍略粗糙的无衬线字，小字号形成左右两组：一组是短注与署名式层级，另一组由日期感数字、短标签、细横线和紧凑正文组成；数字可明显放大作为导航锚点，正文保持短行、松弛行距和轻微手工排版的不齐。文案内容必须服务当前主题，不复制任何来源措辞、品牌或署名；白色字并非纯净发亮，而是带轻微灰度、边缘柔化和印刷渗化，使文字、噪点与摄影颗粒共享同一种旧媒介表面。整体气质克制、孤独、带夜间记录感，让微小亮点、巨大负空间、底部运动与编辑式文字之间的张力成为不可替代的设计手感。\n\n——————\n做成凌晨海岸观测记录海报：以深墨绿为大面积低照度环境，灰青作下部浪沫支撑，唯一暖点用暗琥珀黄，保持窄色域、低饱和、旧媒介颗粒与冷暗包围暖亮的颜色语法。微小灯塔偏右上悬置，视线沿斜向浪脊跌入左下密集区，左上保留巨大空场；主标题在底部左侧以超大两行错位堆叠，日期锚点独立置于右下，形成强烈主次。文案围绕夜航与潮汐观测，画幅为竖版 3:4。\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT6OjDeaQAAQpZU.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT6OjDoboAAn9CM.jpg"]},{"i":18736,"text":"今天努力上架一些新风格\n调试、优化好上传风格流程\n\n甚至整好API来上传风格\n\n本次提示词：\n```\n第一眼形成“巨大柔性体块被超尺度字形与锐利黑色切面共同夹持”的强烈事件：依据未来主题提炼一个圆钝、拱起或弯折的核心形体，将其拆成上下错位且彼此呼应的两段，占据画面中央并主动越界裁切；以纯黑几何楔面从边角斜向切入，在留白中制造紧张的包围、遮挡与方向推力。把目标文字重构为极细至中等粗细、近乎单线性的无衬线视觉骨架，保持正字识别与正常阅读方向，同时拉大字腔、开放端点、克制连接处，让不同字符疏密错落地跨越形体、压住轮廓或被局部遮挡；文字不是说明栏，而是与形体同级的结构梁，字符间允许尺度突变、基线错位和边缘裁切，但不得变成难辨的装饰符号。全局仅用暖白、深黑与颗粒灰，灰色形体通过密集黑白噪点、喷粉般网点和边缘积墨形成由亮心向暗边的粗粝明暗塑形，不使用彩色、光泽、摄影质感或顺滑数码渐变。保留大片不均衡负空间，让圆钝体、尖锐切面、纤细字杆三种形态相互穿插；边缘可有轻微印刷渗散和颗粒抖动，整体像实验性单色印刷成品，冷峻、抽象、克制，拒绝居中规整、完整展示、装饰性美化与精致抛光。\n\n——————\n做成人工智能边界论坛主题海报，画面文字为“智能边界”，采用暖白大底、炭黑切面与银灰颗粒体的高明度无彩关系；核心形体压在右下并向左上反折，左侧形成狭长上升路径，右上保留大块空白；标题拆成跨越上下边缘的超大细字骨架，日期与地点沿左缘小号纵向对齐。画幅为竖版 3:4。\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT6PdaJaEAAy9Bx.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT6PdaNakAINprx.jpg"]},{"i":18737,"text":"Create one independent high-end editorial poster for each uploaded photo. Never combine photos.\n\nFORMAT\nStrict 3:4 vertical composition with an exact 50/50 horizontal split. The top and bottom halves must be equal in height and visually connected as one refined editorial cover.\n\nTOP HALF: ORIGINAL PHOTO\nUse the original photo faithfully. Preserve the subject, identity, facial features, proportions, pose, clothing, objects, composition, lighting, shadows, atmosphere, and color mood. Keep it fully photorealistic with only subtle premium editorial color grading. Never stylize, distort, replace, or alter the main subject. Extend only surrounding background when necessary, seamlessly and naturally.\n\nBOTTOM HALF: HAND-DRAWN ILLUSTRATION\nReinterpret the same scene as a minimalist handmade paper illustration. Preserve the recognizable subject, silhouette, pose, key objects, and main visual story.\n\nUse delicate imperfect lines, simple acrylic-style flat color shapes, visible brush marks, rough paper texture, organic edges, and subtle handmade imperfections. Keep the illustration small and centered, occupying about 10–20% of the bottom half, with generous negative space.\n\nUse a rough white, warm off-white, or pale natural paper background with only minimal environmental details.\n\nCOLOR\nExtract colors from the original photo and reduce them to a maximum of 4 restrained, harmonious colors. Use controlled flat color blocks while maintaining subtle paper grain and brush texture.\n\nTYPOGRAPHY\nOptional minimal editorial text only when appropriate, such as a short title, keyword, location, or number. Keep it understated and never force text into the design.\n\nSTYLE\nQuiet, poetic, refined, minimal, relaxed, artistic, thoughtful, premium, high-recognition.\n\nFINAL\nMaintain the exact 50/50 split. The top must remain a faithful photograph, while the bottom is a simplified handmade illustration of the same scene. Avoid clutter, excessive colors, heavy typography, artificial effects, or unnecessary details. The result should feel like a premium contemporary independent art publication cover.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7Me1qaAAAUZ0F.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7Mfe4bwAAwp10.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7MgUmbEAAXUeR.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7Mg3VbkAAmFuJ.jpg"]},{"i":18738,"text":"Create a premium 3:4 vertical editorial poster using the uploaded photo as the sole reference.\n\nOVERALL FORMAT\n\nThe image must use a strict 3:4 vertical composition divided horizontally into two equal regions with an exact 1:1 height ratio. Each region occupies exactly 50% of the total image height.\n\nUPPER REGION: ORIGINAL PHOTO\n\nUse the original uploaded photo directly as the upper 50% of the composition.\n\nPreserve the subject's exact identity, facial features, body structure, proportions, posture, perspective, clothing, materials, lighting, and original color atmosphere.\n\nDo not regenerate, reshape, distort, stretch, beautify, or alter the subject.\n\nOnly apply subtle high-end color grading, image purification, refined tonal balance, and gentle detail enhancement, giving the image the refined texture of an art magazine or exhibition photograph.\n\nThe background may be moderately expanded to fit the 3:4 composition, but the subject must remain completely unchanged in structure, posture, proportions, and core composition.\n\nLOWER REGION: MINIMALIST INK WASH RECONSTRUCTION\n\nReconstruct the same subject and scene as a minimalist contemporary ink wash artwork.\n\nFirst identify and preserve the most recognizable elements of the original image, including silhouette, outline, structure, perspective, movement, visual rhythm, spatial relationship, and overall atmosphere.\n\nDo not directly copy photographic details. Do not create a realistic reproduction. Instead, translate the original scene into an artistic ink wash interpretation that preserves its recognizable essence and visual relationship with the upper photograph.\n\nUse a milky white, warm white, or natural paper-white base with delicate paper fibers and subtle organic texture.\n\nBuild the artwork using expressive ink wash techniques including dry and wet brushwork, flying white, ink seepage, ink accumulation, soft diffusion, broken edges, layered washes, and intentional white space.\n\nRemove secondary details. Keep only the most distinctive contours, structural transitions, spatial layers, movement, and atmosphere.\n\nThe lower artwork should feel summarized, refined, poetic, and intentionally incomplete rather than realistically detailed.\n\nINK AND COLOR\n\nUse black, charcoal gray, soft gray, and diluted ink tones as the dominant palette.\n\nCreate clear tonal layering with varied ink density, pressure, rhythm, and transparency.\n\nExtract only a few emotionally important colors from the original image and reinterpret them as small areas of artistic staining or pigment.\n\nColors may transform naturally into blue-gray, distant blue, soft gold, warm yellow, vermilion red, light cyan, or similar restrained tones.\n\nDo not mechanically reproduce the original color values.\n\nInk and negative space must remain dominant.\n\nAvoid muddy brown, dull vintage tones, heavy coloring, excessive decoration, or vulgar color combinations.\n\nCOMPOSITION AND NEGATIVE SPACE\n\nThe main reconstructed subject should occupy approximately 30% to 45% of the lower half.\n\nReserve the remaining area for generous negative space.\n\nThe artwork may be asymmetrically positioned, partially framed, suspended, slightly cropped, or offset.\n\nMaintain strong asymmetrical balance and a sophisticated editorial composition.\n\nThe edges of the ink artwork should gradually loosen, fragment, fade, scatter, and disappear into the paper, creating a natural sense of breathing space.\n\nNegative space must function as an intentional visual element, not as empty unused space.\n\nReduce information rather than filling the entire lower region.\n\nThe final lower section should resemble a refined ink seal, contemporary Eastern material study, or museum-quality oriental artwork displayed on a clean editorial page.\n\nTEXT\n\nUse very little text.\n\nDo not add preset titles, numbers, labels, or template typography.\n\nIf appropriate, extract only a few meaningful words or a very short phrase related to the subject, location, time, action, emotion, or metaphor.\n\nPlace the text quietly within the negative space or near the edge of the artwork.\n\nTypography must remain subtle, sparse, elegant, and secondary to the visual composition.\n\nOVERALL AESTHETIC\n\nContemporary Eastern aesthetics.\n\nMinimalist ink wash reconstruction.\n\nPremium art magazine presentation.\n\nExhibition photography quality.\n\nLarge-scale intentional negative space.\n\nSubtle editorial typography.\n\nSmall-scale seal-like visual focus.\n\nQuiet, restrained, poetic atmosphere.\n\nElegant asymmetrical composition.\n\nRefined paper texture.\n\nMuseum-quality visual finish.\n\nAvoid complex backgrounds, excessive photographic details, realistic duplication, decorative clutter, excessive text, rigid template layouts, filled compositions, heavy colors, old-fashioned brown tones, and unnecessary visual elements.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7TR5xaYAAYBLk.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7TR8xawAA4tPr.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7TR5naUAARr_G.jpg"]},{"i":18739,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical surreal travel artwork for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nCreate the entire scene from the written destination alone, automatically selecting its most recognizable architecture, landmarks, landscape, atmosphere, and cultural character.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\n\nBlend a photorealistic historic cityscape with a futuristic long-exposure transformation. The real architecture remains sharply recognizable while selected buildings stretch vertically into elegant trails of white, cream, gold, and warm amber light, creating a surreal double-exposure effect.\n\nCOMPOSITION\n\nBuild one seamless vertical cityscape around the strongest visual identity of [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nPlace a dramatic glowing sun or atmospheric light source in the upper portion against a cool blue-gray sky. Below it, combine authentic historic architecture, streets, bridges, natural surroundings, and a suitable waterfront or reflective surface when appropriate.\n\nLet several prominent structures transition upward into elongated vertical bands of architectural light, as if captured during an extreme long exposure. The effect should grow naturally from the buildings rather than appearing as a separate graphic layer.\n\nREFLECTION & ATMOSPHERE\n\nWhere water is naturally present, create a calm mirror reflection of the architecture, sun, light trails, and surrounding landscape. Keep the reflection slightly softer and more distorted than the main scene.\n\nUse cinematic haze, realistic atmospheric depth, sharp architectural textures, detailed foliage, glowing windows, and subtle motion blur.\n\nCOLOR\n\nContrast a muted blue-gray sky with warm golden, amber, orange, or copper highlights inspired by the destination. Keep the palette sophisticated and cinematic rather than neon or overly saturated.\n\nSTYLE\n\nPhotorealistic architectural photography × surreal double exposure × futuristic long-exposure photography × vertical light streaks × cinematic travel artwork.\n\nThe futuristic elements should feel physically integrated into the real architecture, creating an impossible but believable transformation between historic identity and modern energy.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\n\nDreamlike, atmospheric, sophisticated, cinematic, highly detailed, and unmistakably connected to [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nAvoid generic architecture, invented landmarks, random skyscrapers, excessive neon, heavy glitch effects, cartoon styling, artificial reflections, clutter, collage effects, text, logos, watermarks, borders, and flat digital illustration.\n\nFORMAT\n\n4:5 vertical, single seamless composition, photorealistic detail, dramatic depth, controlled vertical motion blur, cinematic lighting, premium conceptual travel-art finish.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7kKQxb0AANCGd.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7kLD9bUAA9YwI.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7kL0aaYAA-FH-.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT7kMpebQAEiqhy.jpg"]},{"i":18740,"text":"Create a premium 3:4 vertical vintage travel poster for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — create the entire artwork from the destination alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\nReimagine [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] as a cohesive collectible vintage travel poster, using hand-painted gouache and watercolor with a sophisticated mid-century tourism aesthetic.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nUse a warm cream paper background with generous negative space. Place a huge hand-painted destination name across the top in bold, imperfect deep-red uppercase lettering.\n\nBehind the main scene, add a large glowing golden-yellow sun or atmospheric disc. Build the destination in clear overlapping layers — foreground, water/road/landscape, primary landmark, secondary architecture and nature, distant skyline or mountains, then sky.\n\nAutomatically choose 4–6 of the destination’s most recognizable visual elements. Make ONE iconic landmark the dominant focal point and use the others to support the story. Add a characteristic local transportation element when naturally appropriate.\n\nVISUAL STYLE\nHand-painted gouache × watercolor travel illustration × vintage postcard × elegant editorial poster.\n\nUse visible brushstrokes, subtle paper grain, imperfect painted edges, layered washes, simplified graphic forms, crisp silhouettes, selective fine details, and slightly exaggerated but believable proportions.\n\nNo photorealism.\n\nCOLOR\nUse warm cream as the base with a destination-specific palette built around deep red, golden ochre, teal/turquoise, sky blue, leafy green, terracotta, and warm architectural neutrals. Keep the colors rich, harmonious, and distinctly vintage.\n\nATMOSPHERE\nBright, optimistic, nostalgic, and aspirational. Add only a few purposeful clouds, birds, foliage, people, or atmospheric details to give the scene life without creating clutter.\n\nFOREGROUND\nCreate a strong local foreground element — such as a street, boat, train, tram, cable car, road, waterfront, vegetation, or characteristic landscape — with painterly shadows, reflections, and tiny human details.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\nA unified hand-painted travel illustration that feels like a premium vintage tourism poster from a collectible series. Strong hierarchy, layered depth, recognizable silhouettes, balanced asymmetry, elegant typography, and a clear sense of place.\n\nAvoid generic tourist imagery, unrelated landmarks, collage-like composition, excessive tiny details, 3D rendering, glossy CGI, photorealism, modern digital effects, logos, watermarks, and clutter.\n\nFORMAT\n3:4 vertical, single cohesive illustration, premium print quality, sophisticated vintage travel-poster finish.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT8PGyXa4AElg9z.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT8PHdaboAAdjjK.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT8PIZpbMAA2Cpn.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT8PJFJbUAATNBV.jpg"]},{"i":18741,"text":"抓住的不是“水墨滤镜”，而是把照片事实压缩成一枚小型纸境标本：主体缩小、纸层和墨晕形成实体边缘，大片暖白留白承担呼吸感，题签把它固定成一页安静的观察档案。它可泛化到建筑、人物、动物、街景、自然和室内照片。\n\nprompt：\n使用一张输入真实照片，生成一张竖版 3:4 的上下对比编辑手账海报。上半部严格保留输入照片的真实摄影：主体身份、数量、姿态/摆放、关键轮廓、原始光线、视角和背景关系都要准确，照片只做轻微出版物调色，不能画成插画。下半部必须是同一张照片内容的“治愈水彩食物拟人手账”转绘：从原照片提取主体和主要陪衬，把它们重组为米白纸页上的透明水彩插画；保留可辨认的形体、颜色和空间线索，但允许缩小、裁切、留白和改变信息密度。主体可被拟人化为温和可爱的纸上角色，使用极简小眼睛、微笑或困倦表情、淡淡腮红、短手短脚或探出的身体；人物化只能发生在下半转绘区，且不能改变原主体的身份、数量和动作关系。加入细铅笔/针管笔轮廓、半透明水彩晕染、干湿交叠的颜料边缘、纸纤维、轻微水渍和手绘不均匀感。围绕主体只添加从照片事实延伸出的少量手账元素，例如叶枝、果实、餐具、桌面小物、心形、星点、箭头、观察圈和材料字段；不要堆满贴纸，不要套用固定旅游模板。下半部保留大面积米白留白，在纸面上写入少量真实可读的手写英文短标题（优先使用主体名称或场景主题，最多 2–4 个词）、一个小型观察字段和一句极短的温柔观察句；文字像手写在纸上，不能出现品牌、网址、二维码、假中文或长段落。整体像一本安静、温暖、带轻微儿童绘本感的水彩观察手账，色彩从输入照片提取并柔化，保留自然的蓝、红、黄、绿和食物原色，不固定单一配色。\n\n严格版式约束：上下各占约一半，水平分界清楚；禁止左右并排，禁止三联/九宫格，禁止把多张不同照片拼在一起，禁止原图/AI图角标、禁止水印。上半是完整真实照片，下半是同场景同主体的风格转绘，二者必须明显可对照。不要把下半做成原图的等比例描摹；必须通过拟人角色、纸面留白、手写信息和水彩媒介改变主体尺度、信息密度或空间组织。保持所有真实主体的身份、数量、关键动作和主要结构，不凭空增加人物、地点或无关道具。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2wxVqasAA85xe.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2wxVzacAEmbnn.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2wxVuaoAAugXH.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT2wztVaEAAWRUI.jpg"]},{"i":18742,"text":"Create a premium 3:4 vertical editorial travel poster for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nDivide the poster into two seamless stacked halves with no gap.\n\nTOP HALF:\nCreate a full-width photorealistic cinematic travel scene representing [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Automatically choose its most recognizable architecture, surroundings, atmosphere, materials, colors, and natural lighting. Treat this as the authentic photographic view of the destination.\n\nBOTTOM HALF:\nTransform the same scene into a highly detailed isometric miniature diorama viewed from approximately a 45° elevated angle. Rebuild the recognizable architecture, streets, landscape, vegetation, and surrounding elements as a physically believable miniature world on a thin dark-gray rectangular base slab.\n\nMaintain visual continuity between the upper photograph and lower diorama — same architecture, same environment, same lighting mood, and recognizable details — while making the lower section clearly handcrafted as a miniature.\n\nEDITORIAL LAYOUT\nPlace the diorama toward the lower-right area, leaving generous warm off-white negative space around it.\n\nUse thin dark-navy sans-serif typography in the empty space:\n- a poetic 3-line uppercase title\n- “/”\n- a short 4-line travel verse\n- bottom-left: “001” followed by a thin horizontal rule and [CITY / COUNTRY]\n- bottom-right: a thin horizontal rule followed by accurate GPS coordinates\n\nAutomatically determine the appropriate city, country, landmark, and coordinates from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nSTYLE\nPhotorealistic travel photography × hyper-detailed architectural miniature × premium editorial design × quiet luxury travel journal.\n\nUse realistic materials, miniature-scale details, natural shadows, subtle depth of field, warm off-white paper, restrained dark-navy typography, and sophisticated negative space.\n\nThe lower diorama must feel physically constructed rather than like a flat illustration — tiny buildings, roads, vegetation, textures, shadows, and architectural details should have believable scale and depth.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\nMinimal, intelligent, atmospheric, collectible, and highly refined — a contemporary travel journal combining the real destination with its miniature architectural memory.\n\nAvoid collage seams, separate unrelated scenes, generic architecture, invented landmarks, excessive typography, glossy CGI, cartoon styling, clutter, logos, watermarks, borders, and UI elements.\n\nFORMAT\n3:4 vertical, two stacked halves, no gap, upper photorealistic destination scene, lower isometric miniature diorama, premium editorial finish.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT_3aO-a0AAEb7M.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT_3a8pakAAiGma.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT_3b6fbsAEmM3a.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HT_3cn0aIAA18En.jpg"]},{"i":18743,"text":"{\n  \"prompt\"{\n    \"visual_style\": {\n      \"medium\": \"digital painting with hand-drawn ink outlines\",\n      \"aesthetic\": \"modern fashion illustration mixed with graphic novel artwork\",\n      \"texture\": \"visible brush strokes, subtle paper grain, rough painted edges\",\n      \"finish\": \"expressive, painterly, slightly imperfect handmade look\",\n      \"lighting\": \"soft warm ambient lighting with gentle facial highlights\"\n    },\n\n    \"subject\": {\n      \"gender\": \"woman\",\n      \"age\": \"young adult\",\n      \"appearance\": \"attractive woman with natural facial proportions\",\n      \"hair\": \"dark brown, medium-length slightly messy hair with loose strands framing the face\",\n      \"eyewear\": \"large round black-rimmed glasses\",\n      \"expression\": \"calm, slightly confident, relaxed expression with a subtle pout\",\n      \"eyes\": \"light blue-gray eyes, looking toward the smartphone\",\n      \"skin\": \"natural warm skin tone with painterly shading\"\n    },\n\n    \"pose\": {\n      \"framing\": \"vertical medium-to-three-quarter portrait\",\n      \"camera_angle\": \"slightly low-angle selfie perspective\",\n      \"head_position\": \"head tilted slightly backward and toward the camera\",\n      \"body_position\": \"standing casually with relaxed shoulders\",\n      \"right_hand\": \"holding a smartphone near the upper-right side of the frame\",\n      \"phone_position\": \"smartphone raised at approximately face level\",\n      \"left_arm\": \"relaxed naturally beside the body\",\n      \"gaze\": \"looking toward the phone camera\"\n    },\n\n    \"clothing\": {\n      \"top\": \"oversized loose long-sleeve shirt in rich cobalt blue\",\n      \"fit\": \"casual relaxed fit\",\n      \"bottom\": \"dark indigo-blue denim jeans\",\n      \"accessory\": \"small delicate gold pendant necklace\",\n      \"additional_details\": \"warm tan leather shoulder strap visible over one shoulder\"\n    },\n\n    \"smartphone\": {\n      \"type\": \"modern premium smartphone\",\n      \"color\": \"light silver\",\n      \"camera_module\": \"visible dual-camera module\",\n      \"position\": \"held vertically in the raised hand\"\n    },\n\n    \"background\": {\n      \"color\": \"vivid coral-orange\",\n      \"style\": \"flat minimal illustrated background\",\n      \"texture\": \"subtle distressed paint marks, scratches, faded brush patches and paper texture\",\n      \"depth\": \"minimal depth with no detailed environment\"\n    },\n\n    \"composition\": {\n      \"subject_placement\": \"woman centered slightly left of frame\",\n      \"phone_placement\": \"upper-right quadrant\",\n      \"framing\": \"body visible from head down to upper thighs\",\n      \"negative_space\": \"large clean coral-orange areas surrounding the subject\",\n      \"visual_balance\": \"face, cobalt outfit and silver smartphone create the main focal points\"\n    },\n\n    \"color_palette\": {\n      \"background\": \"vivid coral-orange\",\n      \"outfit\": \"rich cobalt blue\",\n      \"jeans\": \"deep indigo blue\",\n      \"hair\": \"deep brown and near-black\",\n      \"skin\": \"warm peach and beige tones\",\n      \"jewelry\": \"soft gold\",\n      \"phone\": \"light silver\",\n      \"overall_palette\": \"bold complementary warm-and-cool color contrast\"\n    },\n\n    \"rendering_details\": {\n      \"linework\": \"loose expressive dark ink outlines\",\n      \"shading\": \"layered painterly shadows with visible brush strokes\",\n      \"facial_details\": \"simplified but expressive eyes, nose and lips\",\n      \"edges\": \"slightly rough hand-painted edges\",\n      \"overall_feel\": \"vibrant, stylish, youthful, artistic and contemporary\"\n    },\n\n    \"negative_prompt\": [\n      \"photorealistic photography\",\n      \"3D render\",\n      \"anime\",\n      \"cartoon character proportions\",\n      \"plastic skin\",\n      \"overly polished digital art\",\n      \"complex background\",\n      \"extra fingers\",\n      \"extra hands\",\n      \"duplicate smartphone\",\n      \"deformed face\",\n      \"distorted glasses\",\n      \"text\",\n      \"logos\",\n      \"watermarks\"\n    ]\n  }\n}","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUACmQiasAAKDOe.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUACnAmawAAjmRL.jpg"]},{"i":18744,"text":"Black and white fine-art architectural portrait photography, vertical 4:5 portrait format. A perfectly circular porthole-shaped cutout reveals a brutalist concrete stairwell, while everything outside the circle is flat, solid near-black charcoal (#161616), with a thin crisp white rectangular border line inset a few millimeters from the frame edge. The circle sits slightly above center, with the thick, weathered concrete ring edge visible on the left side.\n\nInside the circle: wide concrete steps rising diagonally from left to right, a slim dark metal handrail running parallel along the diagonal, a large curved concrete wall on the right catching a hard shaft of direct sunlight that creates a bright white diagonal shape, a dark curved ceiling overhang at the top right, and rough concrete texture on the left wall. Extremely high contrast, deep crushed blacks, bright highlights, strong geometric lines and curves.\n\nA lone man is walking up the stairs in the lower right of the circle, caught mid-step, one hand lightly sliding along the metal handrail. His body is angled up the staircase, but his head is turned and he looks directly into the camera lens, making strong eye contact with the viewer. He is clearly visible, not a silhouette: bareheaded with short dark hair, no hat, no cap, wearing a dark long coat, face lit by the sunbeam on one side, with a calm, serious expression. His face is the sharpest point in the image, with crisp eyes, skin texture, and defined jawline, in razor-sharp focus.\n\nShot on an 85mm f/1.4 portrait lens, shallow depth of field, the stairs, handrail, and concrete walls behind and in front of him fall into a soft, creamy blur, with gentle compression of the stairwell geometry. Moody, minimalist, cinematic, fine film grain, no color, no text.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUADftiacAAhdpF.jpg"]},{"i":18745,"text":"Transform the uploaded photo into a premium editorial scrapbook / torn-paper collage artwork. Keep the main subject of the original photo photorealistic, sharp, and clearly recognizable, with natural lighting, realistic textures, and authentic colors. Place the photo on a warm ivory handmade paper background with subtle paper grain and an imperfect tactile texture. Create an organic ripped-paper transition where parts of the original photograph appear to tear open and naturally continue into the lower area as a minimal hand-drawn ink illustration / sketch, blending the real photograph with the illustrated extension.\n\nAdd subtle vintage editorial details, delicate handwritten-style typography, tiny hand-drawn doodles, imperfect ink lines, small decorative elements, and artistic negative space. Let selected objects from the photograph flow beyond the torn edge and interact with the illustration, creating a playful 3D collage effect. Use soft shadows beneath the paper layers and realistic paper edges for depth.\n\nColor palette: warm cream, beige, muted brown, soft earthy tones with the original photo’s natural colors preserved.\nLighting: warm golden-hour / nostalgic sunlight, soft highlights and gentle shadows.\nComposition: sophisticated, minimal, balanced, artistic, lots of breathing room, premium magazine/editorial aesthetic.\nTexture: handmade paper, subtle grain, torn fibers, slightly imperfect printing and ink texture.\n\nThe final image should feel like a real photograph physically pasted onto handmade paper and partially transformed into a delicate illustration, rather than a digital filter.\n\nImportant: Do not alter the main subject’s identity, proportions, objects, or important details. Avoid excessive decorations, cartoonish rendering, overly clean digital edges, neon colors, or a generic AI-art look. High-end contemporary scrapbook editorial design, photorealistic + hand-drawn mixed-media collage, 4:5 or 3:4 vertical composition.\n\n[OPTIONAL] Add this concept-specific element: [describe the object/scene you want the photograph to transform into]\n\n[OPTIONAL TEXT]: Add a short handwritten phrase: \"[your text]\" in a subtle black/charcoal ink style.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUAMfPIaMAACGGQ.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUAMfQIaUAAxX3g.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUAMfPLbQAAONxl.jpg"]},{"i":18746,"text":"Create a premium 3:4 vertical editorial travel-memory poster for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCOMPOSITION\nDivide the poster into two perfectly equal horizontal halves with no gap.\n\nTOP HALF — CINEMATIC PHOTOGRAPH\nCreate a wide horizontal, photorealistic travel photograph representing [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Automatically choose the most meaningful subject, architecture, landscape, or moment associated with the destination.\n\nThe image must feel like an authentic editorial photograph: natural perspective, realistic lighting, subtle color grading, strong central subject, cinematic atmosphere, and believable environmental details.\n\nBOTTOM HALF — OPEN-BOOK JOURNAL\nCreate one fully opened horizontal hardcover photography book centered in the lower half, viewed almost from above with slight realistic perspective.\n\nThe book should occupy roughly 86% of the lower-half width. The spine must sit exactly in the center, with perfectly equal left and right pages. Show realistic paper edges, thickness, spine curvature, soft shadows, and premium tactile paper.\n\nLEFT PAGE\nFill the entire left page with one dominant color naturally extracted from the destination’s visual identity.\n\nPlace a smaller horizontal landscape photograph at the center of the page, showing the same destination or subject from the upper scene. Keep it rectangular, clean, and surrounded by an even generous border.\n\nRIGHT PAGE\nUse warm ivory paper with abundant negative space.\n\nAt the upper center, add one elegant 3–5 word ALL-CAPS English title inspired by the mood of the destination. Use small black typewriter-style serif lettering with subtle letter spacing.\n\nBelow it, place ONE perfectly upright vintage vertical postage stamp. Give it a cream perforated border, subtle paper texture, and a delicate shadow.\n\nInside the stamp, do not simply reproduce the main photograph. Instead, reinterpret 2–4 recognizable elements from the destination as a playful editorial illustration using bold hand-drawn black outlines, simplified shapes, and ONE bright accent color drawn from the scene.\n\nBelow the stamp, add two short centered lines of gentle poetic English text.\n\nBACKGROUND\nOutside the open book, create a softly blurred continuation of the destination’s environment. Preserve only its general colors, light, and atmosphere while keeping individual objects indistinct.\n\nSTYLE\nCinematic travel photography × contemporary photography monograph × open-book visual diary × vintage postage illustration × minimalist editorial design.\n\nWarm, quiet, sophisticated, tactile, intimate, and collectible.\n\nPRIORITIES\nPerfect 50/50 top-bottom division → perfectly centered book spine → equal pages → strong horizontal photography → intact upright stamp → generous negative space.\n\nAvoid portrait-oriented photo panels, blurred side bars, stretched imagery, invented landmarks, distorted architecture, uneven pages, tilted or cropped books, multiple stamps, excessive decoration, clutter, logos, watermarks, UI elements, or unnecessary typography.\n\nFORMAT\n3:4 vertical, two equal halves, premium editorial photography, realistic open-book construction, refined typography, cohesive travel-journal aesthetic.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUBEs0baUAAcBaN.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUBEtjsbQAA22nJ.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUBEuQrbcAA-4G2.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUBEvBXbgAAh07s.jpg"]},{"i":18747,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical minimalist illustrated travel artwork for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the artwork creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\n\nCreate a warm, whimsical editorial illustration inspired by the mood, colors, atmosphere, and visual character of the destination. Reduce the scene into one charming hand-drawn moment with a simple, storybook-like composition.\n\nMAIN SUBJECT\n\nFeature a small, cute generic illustrated character naturally interacting with the destination environment. The character should have a simple rounded face, tiny expressive eyes, subtle rosy cheeks, and relaxed natural body language.\n\nAutomatically choose appropriate clothing, accessories, pose, and surrounding elements based on [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT], while keeping the character completely original and non-identifiable.\n\nSCENE\n\nBuild a minimal environment using a few recognizable destination-inspired elements — architecture, landscape, flowers, local objects, transportation, food, or cultural details.\n\nDo not overcrowd the composition. Use only the strongest visual elements needed to communicate the location.\n\nSTYLE\n\nHand-drawn children's picture book × soft editorial postcard × crayon and gouache illustration.\n\nUse slightly imperfect outlines, visible crayon strokes, soft gouache fills, simple organic shapes, gentle proportions, subtle paper texture, and charming handmade imperfections.\n\nKeep the background predominantly warm off-white/cream with generous negative space. Add only a few delicate lines, small marks, clouds, leaves, or motion strokes where they improve the composition.\n\nCOLOR\n\nUse a warm, cheerful palette naturally inspired by [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Combine soft cream with a few muted yet lively destination colors.\n\nKeep the palette cohesive and avoid excessive saturation.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC\n\nA charming handmade travel postcard that feels intimate, playful, warm, and artistic — like a tiny illustrated memory from the destination rather than a literal recreation of a photograph.\n\nAvoid photorealism, recognizable real people, copyrighted characters, logos, commercial branding, excessive detail, complex backgrounds, glossy 3D rendering, harsh digital outlines, clutter, text, and watermarks.\n\nFORMAT\n\n4:5 vertical, single illustration, warm off-white paper, generous negative space, cute original character, simplified destination storytelling, premium children's-book/editorial finish.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUCIqvPacAAhH2p.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUCIrk4aMAE5EX0.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUCIsewbgAAwBrD.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUCItb0bgAA4BeC.jpg"]},{"i":18748,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical architectural travel artwork for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate the entire scene creatively from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK] alone. No reference image required.\n\nCORE CONCEPT\n\nTransform the destination into a charming handcrafted miniature world made entirely from knitted yarn, soft felt, embroidery, and plush textile materials. Reimagine its architecture, streets, nature, transportation, and local atmosphere as a sophisticated collectible textile diorama.\n\nLANDMARK & COMPOSITION\n\nAutomatically select ONE unmistakable landmark representing [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / LANDMARK] and make it the central hero.\n\nBuild a complete miniature environment around it using authentic local architecture, streets, gardens, trees, shops, landscape, and a few tiny generic yarn characters. Keep the landmark’s recognizable silhouette and defining architectural features while translating everything into rounded handmade textile forms.\n\nMATERIAL LANGUAGE\n\nEvery element should visibly feel handmade:\n- chunky knitted yarn\n- soft felt\n- embroidered details\n- woven fabric\n- stitched edges\n- wool fibers\n- plush textile surfaces\n- tiny handcrafted imperfections\n\nArchitecture should look carefully constructed from layered fabric and yarn rather than plastic, clay, or CGI.\n\nATMOSPHERE\n\nCreate a warm, playful, cozy travel atmosphere with soft natural lighting, gentle shadows, tactile fibers, rounded forms, and subtle depth. Add small destination-specific details such as local food, transportation, plants, signs, or cultural objects where they naturally enhance the scene.\n\nKeep the background simple and softly colored so the miniature world remains the focus.\n\nSTYLE\n\nArchitectural travel poster × knitted miniature diorama × handmade textile art × plush yarn world × sophisticated editorial illustration.\n\nThe result should feel like an elaborate handcrafted collectible discovered in a miniature museum — whimsical but visually refined and architecturally recognizable.\n\nCOLOR\n\nUse a harmonious palette inspired by the destination itself, combining warm neutrals with a few distinctive local accent colors. Keep the colors soft, rich, and tactile rather than overly bright.\n\nAvoid photorealism, plastic materials, smooth CGI, generic architecture, unrelated landmarks, hard geometric edges, excessive clutter, realistic humans, logos, watermarks, and flat vector illustration.\n\nFORMAT\n\n4:5 vertical, one cohesive miniature world, central landmark, rich textile detail, soft depth of field, premium handcrafted finish, highly detailed yarn and felt textures.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUFCQxgbIAAhuzJ.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUFCRoKagAAHN06.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUFCSVwb0AAQo_q.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUFCTCQbgAAt7bs.jpg"]},{"i":18749,"text":"以参考图人物为原型，保留五官特征、神态、服饰与身体姿态，去除原始背景，重新创作成大师级黑白钢笔人物手稿。采用精湛的传统钢笔绘画技法，以灵动流畅的墨线、细密交叉排线、自然断笔与大胆留白塑造人物的立体感和艺术张力。面部精细刻画，服饰线条疏密有致，局部保留起稿痕迹与随性的未完成笔触，呈现真实艺术家亲笔创作的质感。暖象牙色复古素描纸，清晰可见纸张纤维与细腻墨迹，黑白灰层次丰富。极简艺术画册排版，大面积留白，角落点缀手写签名与创作日期。整体优雅、自由、富有艺术收藏价值，拒绝数字描摹与AI滤镜感，9:16竖版高清构图。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUF9szvboAAV-Hv.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUF9uydagAAsR_a.jpg"]},{"i":18750,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical conceptual travel artwork for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nGENERATIVE IMAGE ONLY.\nCreate the complete artwork entirely from the written [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Do not use, request, require, inspect, modify, or reference any existing image. No source image is needed.\n\nCORE CONCEPT:\nCreate a highly realistic cinematic travel scene combined with oversized white hand-drawn doodle illustrations. The destination itself forms the complete visual foundation, while imaginative white sketch figures interact with the real architecture, landscape, objects, and atmosphere.\n\nDESTINATION:\nAutomatically determine the most recognizable architecture, landscape, streets, structures, transportation, natural features, and cultural details associated with [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Build one coherent scene with accurate perspective, believable materials, natural lighting, and authentic local character.\n\nDOODLE INTERACTION:\nIntroduce only one strong visual idea. Create oversized white hand-drawn figures that actively interact with something naturally present in the scene. They may climb, hold, repair, paint, pull, carry, explore, play with, or transform a real environmental element. Their hands, feet, props, and gestures must connect naturally with the surrounding architecture or landscape.\n\nDOODLE STYLE:\nLoose white marker/chalk line drawings, simple expressive figures, minimal facial features, imperfect hand-drawn strokes, varied line thickness, playful proportions, natural gestures, subtle whimsical character. The drawings should feel like elegant hand-drawn lines existing within the scene, never like stickers, clip-art, comic characters, or 3D cartoons.\n\nCOMPOSITION:\nKeep the realistic destination as the dominant visual layer. Place the white drawings mainly within natural open areas such as sky, water, roads, walls, or atmospheric space. Allow creative scale differences between the drawings and the environment while maintaining believable perspective and spatial relationships.\n\nCOLOR:\nUse the authentic colors and lighting of the chosen destination as the main palette. White linework is the primary graphic accent. Add only a small amount of warm mustard-gold/yellow to selected doodle details such as a prop, light, ribbon, flower, clothing detail, or small object.\n\nVISUAL LANGUAGE:\nCinematic realism × hand-drawn illustration × surreal scale play × visual metaphor × conceptual travel art × premium editorial advertising.\n\nMOOD:\nClever, imaginative, minimal, warm, playful, sophisticated, cinematic, and visually memorable. The concept should be immediately understandable but reveal additional details on closer inspection.\n\nAVOID:\nExisting-image editing, image references, source images, copied photographs, image recreation, photo manipulation, collage, altered landmarks, unrelated architecture, excessive characters, full-screen doodles, thick black outlines, sticker effects, 3D cartoon characters, generic cartoon scenery, clutter, excessive effects, text, logos, watermarks, UI elements.\n\nOUTPUT:\n4:5 vertical composition, ultra-detailed realistic environment, seamless white hand-drawn interaction, premium conceptual travel artwork, polished editorial quality.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUGFaUEbEAEbGo1.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUGFbL_aMAAUKfA.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUGFcBHasAAh05L.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUGFc0LbgAAqlwg.jpg"]},{"i":18751,"text":"```\n围绕任意主题对象生成一张安静、清透、带有水面流动感的视觉画面：主题不以具象物堆叠出现，而是被转译为大面积可呼吸的抽象场域，主体形态由层层横向拖拽的柔软笔触、轻微波纹、半透明色块和边缘参差的负形光带共同塑造。画面第一眼应读到一条从上方缓慢游走到深处的明亮通道，它像光在介质中被折射后留下的空隙，左右两侧以深浅不同的主题色形成温和的图底张力；边界不要硬切，要有被水波拉长、晕开、再收住的节奏。色彩从主题自身的材质、季节、情绪或品牌语义中提取，映射为大面积清透高明度底色、较深的结构暗部、柔和的次级支撑色和少量干净强调色，保持明亮洁净、冷暖轻微牵引、饱和度受控、色阶清晰的关系，避免浑浊、陈旧或灰脏覆盖。文字如果出现，应作为轻量信息层悬停在画面中：主标题居于最安静的视觉停顿处，字距疏朗、笔画干净、白色或主题派生的浅色，辅助信息更小、更轻，整体像漂浮在水面上而不是压住背景。最终画面要有广告级的精确留白、丝滑但可见的手工涂抹纹理、透明层次和克制的仪式感，失败状态是把它做成普通风景、杂乱插画、固定色卡复刻或只剩文字排版。\n\n——————\n主题：节气海报，寒露\n注意：至少8个不同层级的信息点\n\n比例9:16\n一共满足这个主题之下，8种类不同的设计竞标方案， 避免雷同的配色，避免雷同的创意\n```","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUGKVC8bMAAUsUL.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUGKVC6bUAAorL7.jpg"]},{"i":18752,"text":"Create a charming children’s storybook-style illustration of [LANDMARK], inspired by vintage activity-book artwork. Place the landmark in a bright, dreamy countryside or natural setting with soft hand-drawn black outlines, rounded illustrated elements, gentle watercolor textures, and cheerful pastel colors.\n\nThe landmark itself must be highly accurate and realistically depicted, closely matching its real-world architecture, proportions, shape, colors, windows, towers, rooftops, and distinctive details. Do not cartoonize, distort, simplify, or redesign the landmark. It should look like a faithful miniature representation of the actual landmark, while the surrounding environment remains whimsical and illustrated.\n\nAdd a cute little child exploring or looking toward the landmark. Include green rolling grass, a large leafy tree, tiny wildflowers, soft clouds, warm sunlight, and a simple blue sky. No sheep, lambs, or other oversized animals.\n\nKeep the contrast intentional: realistic, instantly recognizable landmark + charming hand-drawn children’s-book surroundings. The child should have expressive innocent features and slightly exaggerated storybook proportions.\n\nVisual style: vintage preschool activity book, soft hand-drawn outlines, watercolor + subtle crayon textures, slightly imperfect printed texture, nostalgic children’s illustration, cheerful and wholesome, detailed environmental elements, realistic landmark architecture, natural lighting, no photorealistic background.\n\nComposition: portrait 4:5, full-page storybook illustration, landmark as the central visual element, child in the foreground, lots of colorful negative space, clean composition, no modern text, no sheep or lambs, no distorted architecture.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUG1nWlbIAA8vkQ.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUG1nWibcAANGrt.jpg"]},{"i":18753,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical travel-editorial artwork for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nPURE GENERATION.\nInvent the complete artwork from the written destination or subject alone. The written destination is the only input. Create every visual element from your own knowledge and imagination.\n\nMASTER STYLE LOCK:\nHand-painted watercolor on warm cream textured paper. Minimalist travel-editorial poster. Transparent watercolor blended with soft gouache. Soft imperfect brushwork, visible paper grain, organic painted edges, muted natural colors, generous negative space, quiet nostalgic atmosphere, sophisticated handcrafted art-book quality. Flat illustrated artwork with painterly depth. No 3D rendering, no glossy finish, no cartoon style, no digital photorealism.\n\nDESTINATION INTERPRETATION:\nAutomatically identify the strongest visual identity of [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Select the most recognizable landmark, architecture, landscape, street character, transportation, vegetation, local objects, or cultural details that naturally belong to the destination.\n\nCreate ONE unified scene rather than a collection of separate elements.\n\nCOMPOSITION:\nUse an elegant vertical editorial composition with one dominant focal point and several smaller supporting details. Establish clear foreground, middle ground, and background layers using watercolor washes and simplified shapes.\n\nLeave generous warm cream space around important forms. Keep the silhouette clean and immediately recognizable. Avoid overcrowding.\n\nLOCAL STORY:\nShow an authentic everyday moment connected to the destination. Include subtle human activity only when it strengthens the story: walking, cycling, sitting, shopping, traveling, eating, working, or simply enjoying the surroundings.\n\nFavor ordinary local atmosphere over generic tourism imagery.\n\nLIGHT & ATMOSPHERE:\nAutomatically choose lighting that suits the destination and scene: soft morning light, warm afternoon glow, misty weather, gentle sunset, or quiet evening illumination.\n\nUse atmospheric watercolor washes to create depth while maintaining a calm, delicate feeling.\n\nCOLOR LANGUAGE:\nBuild the palette naturally from [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Use warm cream, muted ochre, terracotta, dusty blue, soft green, faded red, warm grey, and subtle golden tones where appropriate.\n\nKeep the colors slightly desaturated, harmonious, and naturally layered.\n\nTYPOGRAPHY:\nAt the bottom of the artwork, add three restrained editorial text elements:\n\n[LOCATION NAME]\n[SHORT DESTINATION-INSPIRED SUBTITLE]\n[SHORT WARM POETIC SENTENCE]\n\nUse elegant minimal typography with generous spacing. Keep it secondary to the artwork and ensure all wording is clean and correctly spelled.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC:\nPremium handmade watercolor travel poster × contemporary editorial illustration × nostalgic travel memory × quiet everyday life × sophisticated art-book design.\n\nThe finished artwork should feel like a beautifully remembered place painted by hand: atmospheric, personal, refined, understated, and unmistakably connected to [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nAVOID:\nAny editing workflow, source material, references, existing compositions, copied imagery, collage construction, unrelated landmarks, generic scenery, excessive detail, oversaturated colors, harsh outlines, glossy digital effects, CGI, 3D objects, cartoon characters, clutter, excessive typography, logos, watermarks, interface elements.\n\nFORMAT:\n4:5 vertical portrait composition, warm cream paper, handcrafted watercolor texture, generous negative space, premium print-quality finish.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUHTxopacAAxaN7.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUHTygcbwAEJyG6.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUHTzRnbgAA7RyA.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUHT0CZboAE9JhJ.jpg"]},{"i":18754,"text":"超写实露营地日落画面，年轻女子坐在折叠露营椅上侧身凝视夕阳，黑色长波浪发被微风轻轻吹动，黑色无袖上衣简洁休闲，白色短裤，神态安静放松，中景视角，背景是白色帐篷、草地、远处低矮树影和橙红色天空，夕阳贴近地平线，暖金色逆光勾勒人物轮廓，光线轻柔笼罩整个场景，草地和帐篷边缘有柔和光晕，皮肤在暖光下呈现柔和质感，衣物纹理清晰，画面充满治愈、浪漫和闲适情绪，HDR写实质感，电影级色彩分级，细节丰富","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUHftmhbAAA4R6k.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUHftm6bgAAFAId.jpg"]},{"i":18755,"text":"参考上传的老房子照片，以1:24比例精准复刻为博物馆级超写实实体微缩模型，严格还原建筑结构、屋顶、门窗、墙体及原始环境。精细呈现斑驳墙皮、风化砖瓦、裂缝、青苔、灰尘等岁月痕迹，材质真实自然，具有极致手工制作质感。模型置于精致的矩形沙盘底座上，45度俯视三分之四视角，完整展示建筑全貌。专业微距摄影，柔和自然光，真实阴影，中性灰摄影棚背景，8K超高清。强调真实实体模型效果，避免塑料玩具感、卡通感及3D渲染感。","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUJ6wJZbYAAsbRv.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUJ6yQVakAEp7zs.jpg"]},{"i":18756,"text":"Create a nostalgic editorial scrapbook-style image combining one main photorealistic lifestyle photograph with a hand-drawn illustrated section underneath.\n\nThe top 50–55% should be a cinematic, highly realistic photograph of [SUBJECT / SCENE], captured like an authentic film photograph. Natural candid composition, warm nostalgic atmosphere, soft diffused light, subtle film grain, realistic textures, slightly muted vintage colors, autumnal/warm earthy tones, shallow depth of field where appropriate, beautifully composed but not overly polished.\n\nThe bottom 45–50% should look like a vintage handmade scrapbook / travel journal page, printed on warm cream textured paper. Recreate small elements from the photograph as loose colored-pencil and watercolor doodle illustrations arranged in a clean 3×3 or balanced grid. Include simple hand-drawn objects related to the scene such as [OBJECT 1], [OBJECT 2], [OBJECT 3], [OBJECT 4]. Use imperfect sketch lines, subtle pencil strokes, watercolor bleed, slightly uneven coloring and authentic handmade imperfections.\n\nAdd a short handwritten title at the top of the illustrated section: “[TITLE]”, in casual imperfect black/gray handwritten lettering. Add tiny decorative elements such as hearts, dots, clouds, leaves, stars, waves or small doodles around the illustrations.\n\nAt the very bottom, add a small handwritten caption: “[SHORT CAPTION]”.\n\nOverall aesthetic: cozy Pinterest editorial, nostalgic travel diary, vintage film photography + children’s sketchbook illustration, warm analog memories, premium lifestyle magazine composition, tactile paper texture, understated and elegant, emotionally warm, authentic rather than overly digital.\n\nComposition: vertical 4:5, clean separation between photograph and illustration, balanced negative space, consistent visual storytelling between the photo and drawings.\n\nImportant: preserve realistic photography in the top section; do not turn the photograph into an illustration. The lower section should clearly look hand-drawn. Avoid excessive text, distorted lettering, photorealistic doodles, CGI appearance, oversaturation, clutter, or overly perfect vector graphics.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUKHNs9bsAA5mtE.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUKHNs4bAAEAZvu.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUKHNs2a8AActRf.jpg"]},{"i":18757,"text":"Create a premium 4:5 vertical autumn travel-journal artwork for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY — generate every element from the written destination or subject alone. Do not request, upload, use, or depend on any reference image, existing photograph, or source image.\n\nMASTER STYLE LOCK:\nHand-painted autumn watercolor on warm ivory paper, minimalist travel-editorial illustration, transparent watercolor washes mixed with soft gouache, delicate imperfect ink outlines, visible paper grain, natural pigment blooms, soft edges, muted autumn colors, generous negative space, warm nostalgic atmosphere, premium handcrafted art-book aesthetic.\n\nCOMPOSITION:\nDivide the vertical canvas into two equal halves using a precise 50/50 left-right split.\n\nLEFT HALF — REALISTIC DESTINATION:\nGenerate an original, natural-looking photograph-style scene of [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Automatically determine its recognizable architecture, scenery, atmosphere, and natural lighting. Preserve realistic textures, authentic colors, and believable perspective. Keep this entire half clean, with no text, labels, illustrations, borders, or decorative elements.\n\nRIGHT HALF — AUTUMN WATERCOLOR JOURNAL:\nReimagine the same destination as a delicate, handmade autumn watercolor illustration. Use simplified rounded architecture, warm glowing windows, a small tree with dusty rose, apricot, and amber foliage, a few drifting leaves, and subtle watercolor clouds. Include only a few meaningful local details, keeping the composition airy and uncluttered.\n\nCOLOR PALETTE:\nCaramel brown, dusty rose, apricot orange, creamy yellow, muted maple red, warm ivory, and faint lavender-grey shadows. Use soft, low-saturation afternoon light. No neon colors or harsh black.\n\nHANDMADE DETAILS:\nAdd one or two narrow kraft-brown or dusty-pink washi tape strips, a small pressed autumn leaf, and a few delicate hand-drawn stars or arrows. Integrate these details naturally without overcrowding the illustration.\n\nDESTINATION LABEL:\nPlace a small cream-colored paper label near the upper-left corner of the RIGHT HALF.\n\nMain title: [LOCATION NAME]\nSubtitle: [ENGLISH LOCATION NAME]\n\nUse rounded, handwritten Japanese-inspired lettering for the main title and smaller, widely spaced handwritten English lettering for the subtitle. Keep spelling accurate and typography legible.\n\nSIGNATURE LABEL:\nNear the bottom-right corner of the RIGHT HALF, add a small kraft-paper label with exactly this text:\n\nRYOBIYORI\nNo. [NUMBER] / [YEAR]\n\nUse subtle, fine dark-brown lettering.\n\nSTRICT LAYOUT RULES:\nAll text, labels, washi tape, and decorative elements must remain entirely within the right half. The left half must contain only the original generated realistic destination scene. Never reproduce or modify an existing photograph.\n\nPAPER & FINISH:\nWarm ivory watercolor-paper texture, delicate fibers, subtle grain, organic pigment edges, and a carefully assembled travel-journal feeling.\n\nFINAL AESTHETIC:\nRealistic destination imagery × autumn watercolor illustration × handmade travel journal × nostalgic seasonal palette × premium editorial design.\n\nAVOID:\nReference-image requests, image-editing instructions, existing-photo preservation, unequal panel widths, text crossing the center divider, excessive decoration, oversaturated colors, glossy digital painting, 3D rendering, misspelled text, extra logos, watermarks, and interface elements.\n\nOUTPUT:\n4:5 vertical portrait, exact 50/50 left-right composition, realistic generated destination scene on the left, watercolor travel-journal illustration on the right, ultra-high definition.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUKOKj1akAA9gV6.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUKOLVsbAAADcBL.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUKOMHebQAAvxGJ.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUKONgcbYAAlT13.jpg"]},{"i":18758,"text":"Create a sophisticated contemporary travel-art poster from the uploaded londscape photograph.\nStrict 3:4 vertical format.\nThe upper half must remain the original landscape photogroph. Preserve all important environmental structures, natural textures, lighting, shadows, horizon, architecture, people and perspective. Do not regenerate the scene.\nThe lower half reconstructs the landscape's strongest narrative element using delicate photographic fragments, halftone printing, subtle paper fibers and fading edges.\nUse a single horizontal geometric color field sampled from the landscape. Let the reconstructed subject or horizon physically intersect this field.\nKeep the background most white with muted tones derived from the original image. Avoid saturated colors.\nThe result should resemble a limited-edition museum travel poster rather than a conventional photo collage.","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HULLa9GbkAAQglV.jpg"]},{"i":18759,"text":"Create a premium 3:4 vertical “SECOND WORLD” conceptual surreal photo-collage artwork for [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT].\n\nTEXT-TO-IMAGE ONLY.\nGenerate the entire composition creatively from the written subject alone. Do not request, upload, use, or depend on any reference image or existing photograph. Automatically invent an original scene with authentic photographic realism and a surprising visual concept.\n\nCORE CONCEPT:\nCreate one imaginative “Second World” in which a realistic photographic scene naturally transforms into a delicate, surreal paper-collage world. Discover one unexpected, poetic visual idea inspired by the subject. Make every composition original rather than following a fixed template.\n\nCOMPOSITION:\nDivide the vertical canvas into two connected visual zones.\n\nUPPER 50% — PHOTOGRAPHIC REALITY:\nCreate a believable, high-quality photographic scene inspired by [COUNTRY / CITY / LOCATION / SUBJECT]. Preserve realistic lighting, natural colors, authentic textures, accurate perspective, and atmospheric depth. The scene should feel like a genuine photograph, not a digital painting.\n\nLOWER 50% — THE SECOND WORLD:\nContinue the upper scene onto soft ivory paper. Allow one identifiable element from the photographic scene to cross the center boundary and transform into something unexpected, playful, and visually poetic. The transition must feel physically connected, as though the second world is growing directly out of reality.\n\nCREATIVE TRANSFORMATION:\nInvent ONE distinctive surreal transformation that makes sense within the scene. Explore imaginative relationships between objects, nature, architecture, materials, scale, and physical space. Let the subject determine the concept naturally.\n\nAvoid predictable fantasy structures, repetitive compositions, elaborate architecture, and unnecessary decorative elements. Favor one clever visual idea over multiple competing concepts.\n\nHUMAN & BLACK CAT:\nInclude ONE tiny, clearly recognizable black cat and ONE small, delicately illustrated human figure within the lower world. Give them a meaningful interaction, expressive gesture, or subtle narrative connection to the main transformation. Their poses and relationship should emerge naturally from the scene.\n\nKeep both characters small, charming, and secondary to the central concept. Use thin black-ink outlines with simple, elegant details.\n\nART DIRECTION:\nContemporary surreal editorial collage, authentic photographic realism, handmade paper textures, delicate ink illustration","imgs":["https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HULavtWaMAAB_VM.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HULawgLaYAA3_be.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HULaxRkagAEozaC.jpg","https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HULayBubcAEvN3T.jpg"]}];